        "original_id": "af0548eb-1a61-5e4d-b52e-758db0101e26",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Björn Ulvaeus, Agnetha Fältskog, Benny Andersson, Anni-Frid Lyngstad\n- Organizations: ABBA\n- Places: Stockholm\n- Roles: songwriter, producer, co-composer\n- Works: Chess, Kristina från Duvemåla, Mamma Mia!\n\nFacts:\n- Björn Kristian Ulvaeus was born on 25 April 1945 and was also credited as Björn Ulvæus.\n- ABBA was a Swedish pop group formed in Stockholm in 1972 by Agnetha Fältskog, Björn Ulvaeus, Benny Andersson, and Anni-Frid Lyngstad.\n- Björn Ulvaeus was a member of the Swedish musical group ABBA from 1972 to 1982.\n- Björn Ulvaeus is a Swedish songwriter and producer.\n- Björn Ulvaeus co-composed the musicals \"Chess,\" \"Kristina från Duvemåla,\" and \"Mamma Mia!\"\n- Björn Ulvaeus co-produced the film \"Mamma Mia!\" with fellow ABBA member and close friend Benny Andersson.",
